<TEXT IntroTextLOT none 0>
<TITLE Leaves of Three>
<P 0xFFFFFFFF>
You are Kindred residents of New York City. The Camarilla has a tenuous toehold in the city, a small island with Manhattan, entirely surrounding by Sabbat. The current Prince, the Ventrue Michaela, maintains this area within central Manhattan, staving off nightly Sabbat attacks which test its borders. You know well enough not to venture too close to the thinly guarded borders, as many have met their Final Death on these recent chaotic nights.
<P 0xFFFFFFFF>
Many Kindred complain of the Prince's lack of effectiveness in dealing with the nightly Sabbat barrage, and even whisper of the possibilities of a change in power. Such rumors occur in any city, but due to the circumstances it seems likely that they echo some truth of what goes on within the secret discussions of the Primogen.
<P 0xFFFFFFFF>
You have received a summons to report on the following evening to the Prince's offices within the Barclay South, the upscale high-rise in the Business district that Michaela uses to conduct her Kindred affairs. It's a rather auspicious invitation, one that serves to further your conception of having established yourself as a Kindred of importance within the city. The invitation was delivered by a ghoul introducing himself gruffly as 'Campbell'. In short words, you were instructed to appear at the Barclay's lobby at 11pm the following evening...
</TEXT>

<TEXT MirabilisMurder none 0>
<TITLE The Hit>
<P 0xFFFFFFFF>
You awake from your day's rest to find the hotel in an uproar. Mirabilis has apparently been killed, as his room is awash in blood. Outside his doorway, the young Traci's body was found - mangled beyond recognition. Michaela calls an emergency meeting to discuss the event.
</TEXT>


<TEXT EndTextBadLOT none 0>
<TITLE Chronicle Completed>
<P 0xFFFFFFFF>
Since the coterie hasn't recovered the Blood Pact, you have no proof against the Seneschal. Dominic seems interested in taking you under his wing, although who knows if he simply plans on handing you over to the Triplets, or a bloodthirsty Sabbat war-party? The future certainly holds dangers for the coterie...
<P 0xFFFFFFFF>
The End.
</TEXT>

<TEXT EndTextGoodLOT none 0>
<TITLE Chronicle Completed>
<P 0xFFFFFFFF>
Congratulations! You've succeeded in making your way through the thorny politics of the Kindred unscathed, at least for now. You have earned the respect of the Primogen (except Arianna, who now worries about how much you know of your support of Dominic), and perhaps even Lucinde herself!
<P 0xFFFFFFFF>
The coterie has played a major role in the reforming of the Kindred rulership in New York. Whether this change is for the better remains to be seen...
<P 0xFFFFFFFF>
The End.
</TEXT>

<TEXT EndTextMediumLOT none 0>
<TITLE Chronicle Completed>
<P 0xFFFFFFFF>
Congratulations! You've managed to expose Dominic's treachery, and have earned the debt of Michaela herself! Go carefully now, as these events have earned you allies and enemies in equal parts...
<P 0xFFFFFFFF>
The End.
</TEXT>

<TEXT EndTextNeutralLOT none 0>
<TITLE Chronicle Completed>
<P 0xFFFFFFFF>
You've failed to bring Dominic to justice, but at least you've saved your own carcasses. It will be best now to leave the area, hopefully the coterie can make it out of the city before the Sabbat arrive...
<P 0xFFFFFFFF>
The End.
</TEXT>


